WEBVTT

01:02.020 --> 01:03.730
100 YEARS OF MODERN METEOROLOGY
NEW CHALLENGES

01:11.696 --> 01:13.448
Relationships change.

01:19.704 --> 01:22.665
They either improve or worsen.

01:23.666 --> 01:25.543
They change with time.

01:25.627 --> 01:26.586
And…

01:27.128 --> 01:31.925
they are bound to change
as emotions build up between them.

01:36.012 --> 01:37.305
- Should we include that?
- Yes.

01:37.388 --> 01:39.182
- Like this?
- That's nice.

01:52.737 --> 01:53.822
Dear passengers,

01:53.905 --> 01:58.409
we will soon be landing
at Jeju International Airport.

01:58.493 --> 02:02.455
Please fasten your seatbelts
and open the windows.

02:02.539 --> 02:03.414
Thank you.

02:08.336 --> 02:09.754
What I fear is…

02:10.547 --> 02:12.674
I want to make it work.

02:14.759 --> 02:17.512
I want things to work out between us.

02:18.388 --> 02:19.514
But…

02:21.558 --> 02:23.184
this is all I can do.

02:25.728 --> 02:28.148
Loving someone moderately,

02:28.231 --> 02:30.567
liking them moderately,

02:30.650 --> 02:32.986
and being moderately stable
is what I like to do.

02:34.529 --> 02:37.073
When I go over the line,

02:38.825 --> 02:40.326
I become anxious.

02:43.830 --> 02:45.248
I feel like

02:46.416 --> 02:48.585
I'm a different person.

02:53.965 --> 02:55.758
Get up. Let's go home.

02:56.926 --> 02:58.761
So you decide.

03:00.305 --> 03:02.724
Go to Jeju Island and make a decision.

03:08.396 --> 03:12.901
Think carefully about whether
you can be with me in moderation or not

03:12.984 --> 03:15.445
and make a decision.

03:20.199 --> 03:23.286
…that the minor misunderstandings
and disagreements

03:23.912 --> 03:27.123
affect our relationship
without our knowing,

03:28.124 --> 03:31.252
and they drive us apart.

03:32.837 --> 03:36.090
All that I wanted was this.

03:36.925 --> 03:38.259
I just wanted to have

03:39.761 --> 03:42.472
some personal time with each other.

04:00.073 --> 04:03.284
Where did we go wrong?

04:05.828 --> 04:11.292
How did we end up looking down a path

04:12.335 --> 04:16.172
with no knowledge of what awaits us?

04:22.929 --> 04:26.391
EPISODE 12
VARIATION AREA

04:26.474 --> 04:30.770
WHEN A HOT TYPHOON CHANGES
AS IT PASSES THROUGH KOREA'S COLD AIR

04:30.853 --> 04:34.732
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

04:44.158 --> 04:45.118
Thanks.

04:50.331 --> 04:52.709
I didn't know you loved Si-woo this much.

04:53.376 --> 04:54.836
I don't know anything anymore.

04:55.586 --> 04:58.172
I don't know where it all went wrong.

05:07.890 --> 05:08.891
Director Jin!

05:09.392 --> 05:11.436
You weren't picking up.
I was looking for you.

05:12.020 --> 05:12.895
What's wrong?

05:13.813 --> 05:15.565
There's trouble in the Situation Room.

05:15.648 --> 05:17.066
You should hurry over.

05:18.651 --> 05:20.903
I want to speak to the person in charge.

05:21.487 --> 05:23.614
Where is the person in charge?

05:23.698 --> 05:26.909
- Don't film me!
- I understand, so please calm down.

05:26.993 --> 05:28.661
Let's talk outside.

05:28.745 --> 05:31.706
Calm down? Would you be able
to calm down if you were in my shoes?

05:31.789 --> 05:34.834
My son who was alive and well
is hospitalized right now.

05:34.917 --> 05:37.545
I don't know what happened
or how badly he's hurt!

05:37.628 --> 05:39.380
There's nothing I can do right now.

05:39.464 --> 05:40.631
But what? Calm down?

05:41.215 --> 05:44.260
Damn it. Are you kidding me right now?

05:44.343 --> 05:46.345
How do you expect me to calm down?

05:46.429 --> 05:47.930
That's enough!

05:48.014 --> 05:49.807
Who are you? The one in charge?

05:49.891 --> 05:51.350
Are you? Move aside.

05:51.434 --> 05:53.394
- Move aside.
- What's going on?

05:55.980 --> 05:57.940
Hey. It's you.

05:59.025 --> 06:00.902
I'm Director Jin of Chief Team Two

06:00.985 --> 06:02.445
and Forecaster Lee's superior.

06:02.528 --> 06:04.280
Right. Director.

06:05.406 --> 06:08.034
Did you hear about my son getting hurt?

06:08.868 --> 06:09.869
I did.

06:09.952 --> 06:13.081
When I heard he got hurt
at the typhoon center on Jeju Island

06:13.164 --> 06:16.417
my heart started racing,

06:16.501 --> 06:18.711
and I was so lost!

06:18.795 --> 06:20.838
Let's talk somewhere else.

06:20.922 --> 06:23.091
This room is a restricted area.

06:23.174 --> 06:24.217
What did you say?

06:24.300 --> 06:25.760
Please escort him out.

06:25.843 --> 06:28.387
- Hurry, please.
- Damn it. Stay away.

06:28.471 --> 06:29.931
Don't come near me.

06:30.014 --> 06:32.350
Darn it! Stay away.

06:32.934 --> 06:34.435
Who is he?

06:34.519 --> 06:36.562
Don't come near me. Don't touch me.

06:36.646 --> 06:38.397
Don't you dare touch me!

06:38.481 --> 06:40.066
I'll report you for assault.

06:43.444 --> 06:44.487
Hold on.

06:45.238 --> 06:46.280
Sir.

06:47.281 --> 06:49.325
You're obstructing official duties.

06:49.408 --> 06:51.327
Jeez. So what?

06:51.410 --> 06:52.662
Are you going to sue me?

06:52.745 --> 06:54.539
I'm saying this because

06:54.622 --> 06:56.624
that's how important this room is.

06:56.707 --> 06:59.669
You can't barge in here
and cause a scene. Understand?

06:59.752 --> 07:01.546
- Hey!
- Yes, I'm listening.

07:01.629 --> 07:03.131
My son is important too.

07:03.214 --> 07:06.843
He's my one and only son.
And he's the only son in two generations!

07:06.926 --> 07:08.219
Damn it.

07:11.222 --> 07:14.142
Right. You probably know well.

07:14.225 --> 07:17.145
You and Si-woo
have quite an intimate relationship.

07:17.228 --> 07:18.396
Right?

07:26.154 --> 07:29.615
I'm well aware
that you guys are close enough

07:29.699 --> 07:32.410
to go to motels together.

07:37.457 --> 07:38.374
I see.

07:38.458 --> 07:40.543
Your colleagues don't know, do they?

07:42.587 --> 07:43.421
I get it.

07:43.504 --> 07:45.590
I won't talk too loudly.

07:46.674 --> 07:47.675
Okay.

07:48.301 --> 07:51.512
Anyway, so it's true that you two

07:51.596 --> 07:53.306
are in a relationship, right?

07:58.394 --> 08:00.480
I saw you two at a motel last night too.

08:02.982 --> 08:04.901
Am I wrong?

08:09.447 --> 08:10.740
Please leave.

08:12.325 --> 08:13.242
Answer me.

08:15.786 --> 08:17.830
You can talk with me outside. Okay?

08:22.376 --> 08:23.252
Fine.

08:23.878 --> 08:25.421
We'll talk outside.

08:35.515 --> 08:37.433
I'll take care of it, so stay here.

09:14.554 --> 09:16.514
- Senior Forecaster Um.
- Yes?

09:19.600 --> 09:21.269
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

09:21.352 --> 09:23.896
When did it become like that?

09:31.779 --> 09:33.948
This is Um Dong-han of Headquarters.

09:34.031 --> 09:35.408
We just saw it.

09:36.033 --> 09:37.368
Is it what I think it is?

09:37.451 --> 09:39.704
Yes. It's Typhoon Number 15 Elisha

09:39.787 --> 09:41.247
that followed Number 14 Ricky.

09:41.330 --> 09:45.459
Around 11 o'clock today,
it was moving northeast

09:45.543 --> 09:48.629
with a central pressure of 990mb,
a maximum wind speed of 20m per second,

09:48.713 --> 09:51.757
and a strong wind radius of 150
from 300km west of Okinawa.

10:05.646 --> 10:06.981
Do you have cigarettes?

10:08.983 --> 10:10.568
This is a no-smoking area.

10:10.651 --> 10:13.154
Then give me some coffee or something.

10:18.075 --> 10:22.413
Damn it. The strap broke.
I need money to fix this.

10:22.997 --> 10:24.206
Damn it.

10:33.257 --> 10:34.508
Satellite Center?

10:34.592 --> 10:38.929
At 10 p.m., it'll advance
from 120km west of Okinawa

10:39.013 --> 10:42.516
to the southern sea of Jeju
with a central air pressure of 980mb,

10:42.600 --> 10:46.145
a maximum wind speed of 28m per second,
and a strong wind radius of 200.

10:59.659 --> 11:03.245
16 HOURS AGO

11:19.470 --> 11:20.554
Hey, Bo-mi.

11:21.097 --> 11:23.891
Dad. Were you here all night?

11:24.642 --> 11:26.811
Yes. How are you feeling?
Are you okay now?

11:26.894 --> 11:29.105
I'm fine. My allergies are gone.

11:30.523 --> 11:32.400
The taxi is waiting. Let's go.

11:32.900 --> 11:34.944
Why did you call a taxi?

11:35.027 --> 11:36.529
I could have driven you.

11:37.905 --> 11:39.073
Let's go, Bo-mi.

12:01.846 --> 12:04.932
I think Dad stayed up all night for me.

12:05.724 --> 12:08.519
Don't you think
we should have left with him?

12:08.602 --> 12:10.187
He was never like that.

12:11.480 --> 12:13.899
He never waited for us.

12:13.983 --> 12:15.484
I waited over a decade for him.

12:15.568 --> 12:18.070
So what if he spent the night there?

12:24.869 --> 12:26.620
Get some rest until we arrive home.

12:46.390 --> 12:49.101
Boys, breakfast is ready.

12:49.185 --> 12:50.311
Honey, the food's ready.

12:50.394 --> 12:51.854
- Hurry up.
- It's mine!

12:51.937 --> 12:53.731
Goodness. Hey!

12:53.814 --> 12:56.567
Hey, come here. Goodness. Not now.

12:56.650 --> 12:58.402
Come here right now. Gosh.

12:58.486 --> 12:59.820
Here. Eat first.

12:59.904 --> 13:01.614
- Did you pack your backpack?
- No.

13:01.697 --> 13:02.698
Do it right now.

13:02.781 --> 13:05.159
Put this down. Get dressed.

13:05.242 --> 13:06.202
Get up.

13:08.162 --> 13:09.663
Wait. My notebook.

13:10.581 --> 13:11.540
Your notebook?

13:11.624 --> 13:14.001
- Did you not pack it?
- I don't know!

13:14.084 --> 13:15.211
Where is it?

13:16.003 --> 13:17.421
Eat this.

13:19.924 --> 13:23.385
I'll get you some water.
Put your notebook in your backpack.

13:23.469 --> 13:24.553
Okay.

13:29.808 --> 13:31.519
Honey, aren't you eating?

13:33.354 --> 13:34.313
Honey.

13:37.566 --> 13:39.109
As if it's something so special.

13:40.110 --> 13:42.154
It's only a Grade Five technical exam.

13:44.823 --> 13:46.200
Forget it.

13:47.117 --> 13:48.911
Gyeol! Chan!

13:57.878 --> 14:00.506
Hello, I'm Forecaster Lee
from Headquarters.

14:01.090 --> 14:02.174
How is it now?

14:02.258 --> 14:04.510
As the trough passes through
five kilometers above,

14:04.593 --> 14:06.095
it'll suck in the typhoon.

14:06.178 --> 14:08.806
The typhoon's speed will increase
to 20 or 25km per hour.

14:10.641 --> 14:13.394
The typhoon may hit later at this rate.

14:14.061 --> 14:16.438
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

14:17.147 --> 14:19.608
Hello, I'm Forecaster Lee
from Headquarters.

14:19.692 --> 14:21.694
- Keep talking.
- Sorry?

14:23.195 --> 14:24.363
Well…

14:24.446 --> 14:28.742
I think the North Pacific's anticyclone
located in Japan

14:28.826 --> 14:30.870
isn't moving that quickly.

14:31.704 --> 14:36.166
At this rate, it could slow down
to 10 or 15km per hour.

14:36.834 --> 14:37.793
Look.

14:37.877 --> 14:40.921
Something like this
will barely affect the typhoon's course.

14:41.005 --> 14:44.675
I'm aware that in 2002 and 2014,
the North Pacific's anticyclone

14:44.758 --> 14:47.344
located in Japan slowed down

14:47.428 --> 14:49.889
the speed of the typhoons.

14:51.181 --> 14:53.058
Typhoon Dolphin was the one in 2014.

14:53.142 --> 14:55.436
- And in 2002…
- Typhoon Haishen.

14:56.020 --> 14:58.314
They turned into extratropical cyclones
in variation areas

14:58.397 --> 15:00.441
and only poured
a lot of rain on their way.

15:05.738 --> 15:06.906
What was your name again?

15:08.282 --> 15:12.494
I'm Severe Weather Forecaster
Lee Si-woo from Headquarters.

15:13.495 --> 15:16.123
I'm Sung Mi-jin,
the director of this center.

15:16.206 --> 15:17.583
I'm well aware.

15:17.666 --> 15:20.044
Thanks to you, I'm here one week early.

15:21.545 --> 15:25.090
The climate becomes
more unpredictable every year.

15:25.174 --> 15:26.467
Coming here a week early

15:26.550 --> 15:28.302
will barely make a difference.

15:28.385 --> 15:29.637
What do you need me to do?

15:32.014 --> 15:34.266
We're having a meeting in five minutes.

15:34.892 --> 15:36.101
Yes, ma'am.

15:51.325 --> 15:53.494
- Hello.
- Hello.

15:53.577 --> 15:54.828
Hello.

15:54.912 --> 15:56.288
- Hello.
- Hello.

15:59.416 --> 16:00.250
Hey.

16:00.334 --> 16:02.002
Isn't that Forecaster Lee?

16:08.175 --> 16:09.718
Good morning.

16:09.802 --> 16:12.680
This isn't a good morning at all.

16:12.763 --> 16:14.056
We're expecting a typhoon.

16:15.099 --> 16:17.059
That's exactly why it's a good morning.

16:17.142 --> 16:20.479
I happen to be at the typhoon center
on Jeju Island at this moment.

16:20.562 --> 16:21.897
Don't you feel safe?

16:23.482 --> 16:27.236
We sent you out there to do fieldwork,
and you look even more lively.

16:29.655 --> 16:30.698
All right.

16:30.781 --> 16:32.116
Here comes the typhoon.

16:32.199 --> 16:34.410
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

16:34.994 --> 16:35.953
Sir.

16:36.036 --> 16:38.372
You sent a competent man for once.

16:38.455 --> 16:39.623
Did I?

16:40.374 --> 16:43.460
I didn't send him. Director Jin did.

16:44.253 --> 16:45.629
Director Jin Ha-kyung?

16:46.296 --> 16:48.048
Gosh, what's gotten into her?

16:51.010 --> 16:52.594
Let's begin the meeting.

16:52.678 --> 16:54.346
Satellite Center, are you ready?

16:54.430 --> 16:57.933
There are currently two typhoons
out in the sea at Okinawa.

16:58.017 --> 17:00.561
One of them has
a central pressure of 985mb

17:00.644 --> 17:04.690
and a maximum wind speed
of 25m per second.

17:05.357 --> 17:06.984
Compared to three hours ago…

17:07.067 --> 17:08.402
I like you.

17:13.073 --> 17:15.200
I really like you.

17:16.535 --> 17:18.495
That's why it's too hard.

17:26.545 --> 17:28.130
What's bothering you the most?

17:29.381 --> 17:31.550
You and I are so different.

17:32.968 --> 17:34.928
And I really like that.

17:36.638 --> 17:38.766
But it's giving me a hard time.

17:54.865 --> 17:58.619
At this rate, the typhoon
will affect us tomorrow afternoon.

17:58.702 --> 18:00.746
It has indeed increased in speed.

18:00.829 --> 18:04.249
But the current sea temperature
in the southwest region is 26 to 27°C.

18:04.333 --> 18:05.626
The ocean heat content

18:05.709 --> 18:08.087
and the vertical wind shear
are both under ten units.

18:08.170 --> 18:11.965
The environment isn't suitable
for the typhoon to develop yet.

18:13.634 --> 18:14.676
Typhoon Center.

18:14.760 --> 18:18.597
What's your take on how the typhoon
isn't getting enough energy?

18:19.556 --> 18:23.435
The ocean heat content can increase
since it's still morning.

18:24.019 --> 18:28.107
Plus, the sea surface temperature
is 3°C higher than last year's.

18:28.190 --> 18:30.776
At this rate, it's highly likely

18:30.859 --> 18:33.195
that it'll receive energy in our waters.

18:35.572 --> 18:38.367
How powerful will it be
when it hits our land?

18:38.450 --> 18:40.285
By that time,

18:40.369 --> 18:44.414
its CI value will be 2.5 to 3.0.

18:44.498 --> 18:48.377
As of now, we can expect it to hit Mokpo.

18:48.460 --> 18:49.711
Correct.

18:49.795 --> 18:54.007
When the typhoon hits Mokpo,
the central pressure will be 970mb

18:54.091 --> 18:58.178
and the maximum wind speed
will be at least 30m per second.

18:59.054 --> 19:01.223
This could be more destructive

19:01.306 --> 19:03.642
than Typhoon Prapiroon of 2018.

19:03.725 --> 19:06.895
AVERAGE DIFFERENCES
IN SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES

19:17.614 --> 19:18.782
Oh, dear.

19:25.706 --> 19:29.376
Typhoon Ricky, the 14th typhoon,
is moving north toward Korea.

19:29.459 --> 19:31.920
The eye of the typhoon is very clear

19:32.004 --> 19:34.089
which shows how powerful the typhoon is.

19:34.173 --> 19:37.050
In the center of the typhoon is a gale

19:37.134 --> 19:39.094
with a speed of 100km per hour.

19:40.971 --> 19:43.098
It's important to know
the path of the typhoon…

19:43.182 --> 19:44.474
- Mom.
- Yes?

19:44.558 --> 19:47.019
Do you know how fast 100km per hour is?

19:48.103 --> 19:49.313
I'm not sure.

19:49.897 --> 19:52.858
The distance between Seoul
and Jeonju is about 200km.

19:52.941 --> 19:55.444
That means we can get there
in just two hours.

19:56.028 --> 19:57.321
Isn't that crazy?

19:57.404 --> 19:59.198
That was impressive.

19:59.281 --> 20:01.575
I learned this during my KMA field trip.

20:01.658 --> 20:04.119
Stay on high alert in dangerous areas

20:04.912 --> 20:06.413
and make sure to avoid injuries.

20:06.496 --> 20:09.041
Those in farming areas
should avoid outdoor activities…

20:09.124 --> 20:11.960
Dad was actually pretty impressive

20:12.044 --> 20:13.420
when I got to see him work.

20:16.340 --> 20:19.760
Why did you eat the ham
when you knew you shouldn't?

20:19.843 --> 20:21.220
It just slipped my mind.

20:22.137 --> 20:23.764
How could you forget that?

20:24.348 --> 20:27.142
You went to the emergency center
when you were young

20:27.226 --> 20:28.977
because you ate gimbap that had ham.

20:32.606 --> 20:33.523
I'm hungry.

20:34.107 --> 20:35.651
Do we have anything to eat?

20:40.364 --> 20:41.823
Don't visit him again.

20:42.407 --> 20:44.618
He's busy during
the disaster prevention season.

20:48.205 --> 20:51.041
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

20:52.376 --> 20:53.961
It's time for your medication.

20:54.044 --> 20:55.754
Do you see it on the table?

20:57.756 --> 20:59.633
- Mom.
- Yes?

21:01.718 --> 21:02.928
Are you getting a divorce?

21:14.898 --> 21:16.483
Take your medication.

21:43.051 --> 21:44.303
How's your daughter?

21:45.137 --> 21:47.347
She was discharged early in the morning.

21:49.349 --> 21:50.350
That's a relief.

21:50.434 --> 21:52.352
There must have been
a lot to take care of.

21:52.436 --> 21:55.188
Her mom was the one
who took care of everything.

21:56.898 --> 21:59.985
My entire life has been futile.

22:01.111 --> 22:04.364
I was always proud
of how hardworking I was.

22:05.407 --> 22:06.700
But looking back,

22:06.783 --> 22:09.119
I was nothing but a lousy dad.

22:09.202 --> 22:13.123
I had no idea she was allergic
and fed her that ham.

22:14.374 --> 22:17.419
Gosh. I put my only daughter in danger.

22:22.132 --> 22:25.052
There are various types of dads.

22:25.927 --> 22:28.722
Having a considerate dad is great.

22:29.514 --> 22:33.727
But I think a dad who lives his life
to the fullest is also a good dad.

22:36.229 --> 22:37.355
Are you comforting me?

22:38.565 --> 22:39.941
Did it work?

22:40.025 --> 22:41.026
Yes.

22:44.321 --> 22:45.447
Don't worry.

22:46.198 --> 22:50.327
Gosh. Two typhoons are around the corner,
so I need to be on my toes.

22:50.911 --> 22:54.122
You're right. And one of them
is stronger than Typhoon Prapiroon.

22:54.206 --> 22:57.918
By the way, you had great foresight.

22:58.794 --> 23:00.921
You sent Forecaster Lee down there.

23:02.714 --> 23:04.633
Right. It just happened that way.

23:11.431 --> 23:13.433
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

23:13.517 --> 23:15.143
- Thank you.
- Bye.

23:20.023 --> 23:22.567
How many casualties
were there during Typhoon Prapiroon?

23:22.651 --> 23:24.569
Thirty-eight deaths and missing persons,

23:24.653 --> 23:26.530
and 366 injured.

23:26.613 --> 23:29.032
There must have been
serious property damage.

23:29.116 --> 23:32.577
Seventy billion won just in Seoul.
But casualties are the biggest problem.

23:33.245 --> 23:35.747
By the way, is Reporter Chae okay?

23:37.833 --> 23:39.501
I haven't seen her lately.

23:40.085 --> 23:43.171
Right. She wanted a break,
so I told her to take one.

23:45.048 --> 23:46.258
Are you guys…

23:48.051 --> 23:49.094
What?

23:49.761 --> 23:51.680
Getting ready to have a baby?

23:56.101 --> 23:58.103
- Assistant Director Kim.
- Yes?

23:58.186 --> 24:00.981
Shouldn't you inform the press
about the briefing time?

24:01.773 --> 24:03.817
Right. I'm so out of it.

24:30.635 --> 24:32.137
Dong-jin.

24:32.220 --> 24:33.305
Yu-jin!

24:34.264 --> 24:36.725
Goodness. Come on!

24:37.517 --> 24:39.186
How have you been, kid?

24:39.269 --> 24:40.812
Took you long enough.

24:41.396 --> 24:44.065
- I missed you so much.
- Did you?

24:44.774 --> 24:47.277
Gosh. You've grown a lot
since I last saw you.

24:49.279 --> 24:50.906
- Hey, you're here.
- Hey.

24:52.157 --> 24:53.325
Where's his dad?

24:53.408 --> 24:55.327
He's moving his boat
before the typhoon hits.

24:55.410 --> 24:56.870
- Come in.
- Okay.

24:58.205 --> 24:59.289
Let's go.

25:05.337 --> 25:09.132
JEJU OFFICE

25:10.967 --> 25:13.553
Make sure the AWS is
functioning properly first.

25:13.637 --> 25:14.679
Yes, sir.

25:15.931 --> 25:18.850
- Are you going too?
- I'll be here for some time,

25:18.934 --> 25:20.936
so I should know where they're stationed.

25:21.019 --> 25:23.939
Gosh, you're hardworking.
Don't work too late.

25:24.022 --> 25:25.899
- Okay.
- Let's go.

25:26.858 --> 25:27.776
Please.

25:33.782 --> 25:35.116
What's going on?

25:35.200 --> 25:36.826
It slowed down significantly.

25:36.910 --> 25:39.871
They're analyzing it
but haven't found the cause yet.

25:40.830 --> 25:43.583
It stopped in the sea
southwest of Jeju for an hour now.

25:44.626 --> 25:46.670
What's going on this time? Tell me.

25:47.420 --> 25:50.757
The typhoon has come
to a standstill in the Jeju sea.

25:50.840 --> 25:52.509
We're looking into the cause.

25:53.468 --> 25:55.553
Oh, dear.

25:59.391 --> 26:03.645
It's 7 p.m. right now.
Typhoon Ricky suddenly turned east

26:03.728 --> 26:06.231
and is currently
in the southwest seas of Jeju.

26:06.940 --> 26:09.359
Could its upper and lower parts
have separated

26:09.442 --> 26:11.403
and affected its movement?

26:11.486 --> 26:12.737
That could be possible,

26:12.821 --> 26:15.532
but we can't tell
with the current satellite images.

26:17.993 --> 26:21.037
I'd like to see
the current adiabatic chart there.

26:21.121 --> 26:22.831
Could you carry out a special observation?

26:22.914 --> 26:27.043
Then we need to do
a sonde observation from Seongsan.

26:27.127 --> 26:28.670
Our observation vehicle is there.

26:28.753 --> 26:32.799
Our observation vehicle is
around there as we speak.

26:33.383 --> 26:35.593
Sir, should we do it?

26:38.805 --> 26:41.141
Will you be able to tell
with the adiabatic chart?

26:41.725 --> 26:43.184
Yes. The upper and lower parts

26:43.268 --> 26:45.687
and the wind five kilometers above
need to be checked.

26:51.109 --> 26:53.945
SPECIAL OBSERVATION VEHICLE

27:12.255 --> 27:13.465
Sir.

27:13.548 --> 27:16.634
How many AWSs are on Jeju Island?

27:16.718 --> 27:17.969
Twenty-five in total.

27:18.053 --> 27:19.220
I see.

27:19.971 --> 27:21.723
Are we checking all of them today?

27:21.806 --> 27:24.309
Come on.
This island is too big to do that.

27:24.392 --> 27:27.270
We're in a hurry, so we'll only check
the eight in the eastern region.

27:27.354 --> 27:28.772
I see.

27:33.026 --> 27:34.319
Let's go.

27:34.986 --> 27:36.529
What? Si-woo.

27:38.823 --> 27:40.367
Why are you here?

27:40.450 --> 27:43.203
Well, I'm visiting my mom.

27:45.038 --> 27:47.540
She's my mom, and he's my brother.

27:47.624 --> 27:49.250
Hello.

27:50.085 --> 27:52.003
- Hi.
- Why are you here?

27:52.087 --> 27:54.214
I was dispatched to the typhoon center.

27:54.297 --> 27:55.382
Hey.

27:55.465 --> 27:57.467
- Do you work at the KMA?
- Yes.

27:58.051 --> 27:59.219
That's where I work.

27:59.803 --> 28:02.097
Are you her boyfriend?

28:02.180 --> 28:03.681
- What?
- Goodness.

28:03.765 --> 28:05.809
Don't be silly. She's already married.

28:05.892 --> 28:08.353
You've seen your brother-in-law.

28:08.436 --> 28:09.938
You're right.

28:12.482 --> 28:15.068
Forecaster Lee, Director Sung just called.

28:15.151 --> 28:17.070
We need to do
a sonde observation in Seongsan.

28:17.654 --> 28:18.947
I see. Right now?

28:19.030 --> 28:22.033
Yes. The typhoon is being erratic.

28:22.117 --> 28:23.910
I want to tag along!

28:24.411 --> 28:25.954
Goodness, Dong-jin.

28:28.206 --> 28:30.708
I want to go with you.

28:30.792 --> 28:32.794
Yu-jin, can I tag along with him?

28:32.877 --> 28:34.587
No, they need to work.

28:34.671 --> 28:37.841
I want to go. Please.

28:37.924 --> 28:39.050
I want to go.

28:39.134 --> 28:41.469
Can they tag along

28:41.553 --> 28:43.096
and watch us from afar?

28:50.270 --> 28:51.354
Can they?

29:01.406 --> 29:04.367
- What a surprise.
- Did you hear about the typhoon?

29:04.451 --> 29:06.369
Took you long enough to call.

29:06.453 --> 29:08.121
The morning news

29:08.204 --> 29:11.374
kept telling us to be prepared for it.

29:13.042 --> 29:14.919
Okay. I'm hanging up.

29:15.003 --> 29:18.298
Hey. I have something
to ask you too, okay?

29:18.381 --> 29:20.049
What is it?

29:22.886 --> 29:24.220
It's about that guy.

29:24.888 --> 29:26.514
I'm hanging up
if it's about Assistant Shin.

29:26.598 --> 29:29.559
No, not him.

29:29.642 --> 29:34.022
I'm talking about that pale-faced guy
who's staying at your place.

29:34.105 --> 29:35.732
Was his name Lee Si-woo?

29:36.524 --> 29:37.650
What about him?

29:39.110 --> 29:40.403
Did he mention me?

29:40.987 --> 29:42.447
Why would he?

29:42.530 --> 29:45.116
Did something happen again?

29:45.200 --> 29:47.577
We had dinner together. So what?

29:47.660 --> 29:50.455
Why would you eat with him? When?

29:50.538 --> 29:51.748
I mean… Why?

29:51.831 --> 29:53.666
Why would you eat together?

29:53.750 --> 29:56.377
Then what could I have done?
You weren't picking up,

29:56.461 --> 29:58.505
and I was dying
to know about the guy upstairs.

29:58.588 --> 30:01.549
Don't tell me you mentioned
Assistant Director Shin and me to him.

30:01.633 --> 30:06.429
Then you should have picked up my call.

30:07.430 --> 30:09.307
What could I do? You weren't answering.

30:09.891 --> 30:12.393
But still, that's not right.

30:12.477 --> 30:15.188
Why not? His director's mother

30:15.271 --> 30:17.148
treated him to dinner.

30:17.232 --> 30:19.150
Why is that such a big deal?

30:23.404 --> 30:25.490
Times have changed, Mom.

30:25.573 --> 30:28.493
You can't just meet up with my subordinate

30:28.576 --> 30:30.411
and ask them personal questions.

30:31.162 --> 30:33.748
Do this once more,
and I'll never see you again.

30:33.832 --> 30:37.210
Goodness. Calm down, will you?

30:38.586 --> 30:39.587
Hey.

30:41.005 --> 30:44.050
Did you catch onto it as well?

30:44.133 --> 30:45.301
Catch onto what?

30:45.885 --> 30:48.555
I think that guy likes you.

30:52.934 --> 30:55.061
By the looks of it,

30:55.144 --> 30:57.480
I think he's… What's the word again?

30:57.564 --> 30:58.940
Right. Adoration.

30:59.023 --> 31:02.277
I think he adores you.

31:04.779 --> 31:07.156
Hello?

31:07.240 --> 31:08.867
Hey, did you hang up?

31:10.660 --> 31:12.370
Unbelievable.

31:16.082 --> 31:17.667
MOM

31:22.922 --> 31:24.299
What's going on with them?

31:24.799 --> 31:27.552
Is the feeling mutual?

31:28.553 --> 31:31.264
No way. That can't be.

31:31.848 --> 31:34.809
It's possible with Tae-kyung,
but not Ha-kyung.

31:34.893 --> 31:37.228
She always opts for a safer choice.

31:50.033 --> 31:51.367
Doors opening.

32:00.627 --> 32:01.794
Doors closing.

32:04.380 --> 32:06.633
- Going home?
- Yes.

32:07.884 --> 32:10.678
- Working late?
- Yes. I'm going out for dinner.

32:11.179 --> 32:12.305
I see.

32:19.646 --> 32:20.939
Can I join?

32:40.750 --> 32:43.670
- It's pretty windy.
- You're right.

32:45.004 --> 32:46.965
DATE OF DATA
JULY 30, 2022

32:55.807 --> 32:57.600
Just call him first.

32:58.226 --> 33:01.437
- What do you mean?
- I know you're waiting for Ki-jun to call.

33:01.521 --> 33:02.814
How did you know?

33:02.897 --> 33:05.483
It's obvious. I could tell.

33:07.819 --> 33:11.239
You shouldn't drag on your fights
when you're married.

33:11.990 --> 33:15.118
It's best that you call him, make up,

33:15.201 --> 33:16.536
and leave tomorrow morning.

33:17.161 --> 33:19.622
Mom. I arrived here today.

33:19.706 --> 33:22.417
You guys can visit me during Thanksgiving.

33:24.293 --> 33:25.628
What's wrong?

33:25.712 --> 33:29.298
Are you afraid that
my first marriage will fail like yours?

33:31.592 --> 33:32.760
Yes.

33:34.012 --> 33:35.054
I'm afraid.

33:36.347 --> 33:40.101
I got married when I was young
and didn't know any better.

33:41.102 --> 33:43.771
That's why we clashed even more.

33:44.355 --> 33:46.441
Forget it. I don't want to hear it.

33:49.318 --> 33:52.530
Ki-jun is a good person. I can see that.

33:53.948 --> 33:55.700
I don't know what it's about,

33:55.783 --> 33:57.577
but just give in. Okay?

33:58.828 --> 34:01.122
Extend an olive branch.

34:03.374 --> 34:05.126
I'll take care of it.

34:05.877 --> 34:06.794
So stop.

34:15.386 --> 34:16.345
Care for a drink?

34:17.180 --> 34:19.223
I need to go back to the Situation Room.

34:19.307 --> 34:20.933
Two typhoons are headed our way.

34:33.029 --> 34:35.156
Am I really that dense, Ha-kyung?

34:37.909 --> 34:41.621
Am I really that untrustworthy
and difficult to deal with?

34:44.707 --> 34:46.125
Was I really that terrible?

34:47.585 --> 34:49.170
Was I that irritable

34:49.253 --> 34:51.255
and contemptible?

34:52.757 --> 34:53.883
Well…

34:53.966 --> 34:56.344
I can't completely deny that.

34:56.427 --> 34:58.346
But overall,

34:58.429 --> 35:00.515
you're a pretty decent woman.

35:01.474 --> 35:02.809
You're competent,

35:02.892 --> 35:05.269
responsible, and take
great care of yourself.

35:06.062 --> 35:09.273
As long as it wasn't work-related,

35:09.357 --> 35:11.692
you were considerate toward me.

35:11.776 --> 35:13.194
It's just that

35:13.820 --> 35:16.239
we weren't meant to be.

35:17.657 --> 35:18.783
You're not bad yourself.

35:19.450 --> 35:21.911
You're hardworking, devoted to your job,

35:21.994 --> 35:24.038
clear-cut, and know exactly what you want.

35:24.997 --> 35:28.417
Well, I can't deny
that you can be dense at times.

35:29.877 --> 35:31.129
But you weren't that bad.

35:33.923 --> 35:36.592
It's just that we weren't the best fit.

35:41.139 --> 35:44.058
I had no idea
that's how you thought of me.

35:45.226 --> 35:46.435
To be honest,

35:46.519 --> 35:50.565
I thought you always looked down on me.

35:50.648 --> 35:52.817
"Gosh, he's such an idiot."

35:52.900 --> 35:55.319
"Is there anything he can do?" Like this.

35:56.863 --> 35:58.823
I just wished you'd do better.

35:58.906 --> 36:00.533
I didn't mean you were incompetent.

36:05.621 --> 36:07.832
Why couldn't we have
told each other this sooner?

36:10.877 --> 36:13.629
Because we didn't think
we had to say it out loud.

36:14.255 --> 36:15.798
But I had no idea.

36:16.507 --> 36:17.925
That's why I misunderstood you.

36:18.926 --> 36:20.136
Countless times.

36:20.720 --> 36:21.804
You're right.

36:22.430 --> 36:26.475
There are many things
we wouldn't know unless we express them.

36:30.146 --> 36:33.608
There are many things
we wouldn't know unless we express them.

36:36.152 --> 36:37.612
So why did we expect each other

36:37.695 --> 36:41.032
to realize those things
without saying anything?

36:48.414 --> 36:50.041
What? It's raining.

36:50.124 --> 36:51.918
Forecaster Lee, give me a minute.

36:52.001 --> 36:52.960
Okay.

37:09.268 --> 37:11.145
HIGH PURITY HYDROGEN

37:47.556 --> 37:48.557
Where are you?

37:48.641 --> 37:50.685
Can you at least tell me where you are?

38:40.401 --> 38:41.569
Si-woo…

38:45.948 --> 38:46.866
Si-woo!

38:49.410 --> 38:50.494
Si-woo!

38:51.412 --> 38:53.581
- Si-woo, are you okay?
- Forecaster Lee!

38:53.664 --> 38:55.249
- Si-woo!
- Forecaster Lee!

38:55.333 --> 38:57.543
Oh, no. 911!

38:57.626 --> 38:58.878
Stay awake!

39:05.551 --> 39:06.927
I wonder how badly he's hurt.

39:07.011 --> 39:10.222
PRESENT

39:11.098 --> 39:13.184
Can you call the hospital in Jeju again?

39:13.267 --> 39:14.226
Sorry?

39:14.310 --> 39:16.354
I want to check on Forecaster Lee.

39:16.437 --> 39:18.731
- Please call them.
- Yes, ma'am.

39:25.821 --> 39:28.657
Based on the last report we received,

39:28.741 --> 39:31.494
he's thankfully
not in a critical condition.

39:32.953 --> 39:33.996
So?

39:35.456 --> 39:37.458
- Sorry?
- Are you saying

39:38.042 --> 39:40.419
you won't compensate for what has happened

39:40.503 --> 39:43.589
because he's no longer
in critical condition? Is that it?

39:44.340 --> 39:45.549
No, sir.

39:46.217 --> 39:48.928
We will compensate
for our employee's injuries.

39:49.553 --> 39:53.015
I only said that
because I thought you'd be curious.

39:53.099 --> 39:54.934
Are you serious right now?

39:55.768 --> 39:57.686
Listen up, Mr. Civil Servants.

39:57.770 --> 39:58.813
I know

39:59.313 --> 40:01.899
you're just trying to cover up

40:01.982 --> 40:03.609
and mitigate the situation.

40:03.692 --> 40:05.361
But it won't work on me!

40:05.861 --> 40:09.156
Excuse me.
You should be careful of what you say.

40:09.240 --> 40:10.324
I don't want to hear it!

40:11.409 --> 40:13.953
Anyway, let's get this compensation issue

40:14.036 --> 40:16.580
cleared up before moving on.

40:17.456 --> 40:18.624
Okay, sir.

40:21.252 --> 40:22.461
Come in.

40:23.838 --> 40:24.964
What is it?

40:25.047 --> 40:27.967
I called the hospital a minute ago.

40:28.050 --> 40:29.969
He was just moved to a general ward.

40:30.052 --> 40:32.263
- His eyes are slightly injured.
- Wait.

40:33.097 --> 40:34.890
He hurt his eyes?

40:36.350 --> 40:37.393
That means…

40:39.812 --> 40:43.149
Do you know that means
a class one disability?

40:44.483 --> 40:47.278
Not everyone who's injured
becomes disabled.

40:47.361 --> 40:49.864
I know you're his father,
but you're taking this too far.

40:49.947 --> 40:51.615
What are you talking about?

40:51.699 --> 40:53.701
It's you people
who are stepping over the line.

40:54.368 --> 40:57.663
You put him in danger,
and now, he's incapacitated.

40:57.746 --> 41:00.708
Shouldn't the government
take responsibility for it?

41:00.791 --> 41:02.710
Am I wrong?

41:04.295 --> 41:06.088
No, sir. You're right.

41:06.172 --> 41:07.173
Right?

41:07.798 --> 41:09.967
She and I see eye to eye.

41:10.050 --> 41:11.302
Speaking of which,

41:11.385 --> 41:12.928
let's go to Jeju Island together.

41:14.680 --> 41:15.723
What?

41:16.307 --> 41:17.808
We should go there

41:17.892 --> 41:19.477
and see how he's doing.

41:19.560 --> 41:21.729
After that, we can discuss what to do.

41:28.861 --> 41:29.695
Director Jin.

41:29.778 --> 41:32.740
He's your only son
and the only son in two generations.

41:33.532 --> 41:34.492
Exactly.

41:35.367 --> 41:38.662
That's why I'd like to clear up
this compensation issue right now

41:38.746 --> 41:40.539
for my son's sake.

41:40.623 --> 41:44.084
But first, you should check on him.

41:45.336 --> 41:48.797
That way, we can figure out
how much to compensate.

41:52.343 --> 41:54.512
I'd like to take
the first flight out tomorrow.

41:54.595 --> 41:56.096
Would that be okay, sir?

41:56.180 --> 41:58.474
Yes. Of course.

41:59.099 --> 42:00.684
Will you be all right?

42:01.310 --> 42:02.436
Of course.

42:03.479 --> 42:05.064
See you at the airport tomorrow.

42:18.869 --> 42:19.912
What?

42:21.080 --> 42:22.873
Why would you go with them?

42:22.957 --> 42:26.418
If they need someone,
the Management Support Team will go.

42:26.502 --> 42:28.462
There's something urgent I must do.

42:29.046 --> 42:30.005
No.

42:30.089 --> 42:32.591
Two typhoons are headed our way.

42:33.217 --> 42:34.802
Can I really not go, sir?

42:35.594 --> 42:37.555
No. You can't.

42:39.014 --> 42:41.976
Then I'd like to take a leave.

42:42.643 --> 42:44.478
- What did you say?
- The typhoons?

42:45.187 --> 42:46.313
Sure, they're important.

42:46.397 --> 42:47.982
And so are the people's safety.

42:48.065 --> 42:51.485
But I've never taken a leave
during the disaster prevention season

42:51.569 --> 42:53.362
while working here.

42:53.445 --> 42:55.072
I never took a single leave.

42:55.573 --> 42:56.991
Not even a half-day.

42:57.074 --> 42:58.534
I worked like a dog.

42:58.617 --> 43:00.619
And so did everyone else.

43:00.703 --> 43:01.787
Exactly.

43:01.870 --> 43:05.749
Everyone here has a sense of duty,
and I'm not the only one on our team.

43:06.500 --> 43:09.044
So please let me go this once.

43:09.128 --> 43:11.422
But why does it have to be right now?

43:11.505 --> 43:12.631
Beats me.

43:13.591 --> 43:15.718
Yu-jin just happened
to leave me right now.

43:18.304 --> 43:19.138
What?

43:19.722 --> 43:21.098
Is that why

43:21.181 --> 43:23.559
I haven't been seeing her lately?

43:26.353 --> 43:30.149
My entire marriage is at stake here.

43:32.192 --> 43:33.527
Please let me go.

43:34.445 --> 43:36.530
Gosh.

43:44.705 --> 43:46.040
Director Jin.

43:46.874 --> 43:50.377
I'll join you on that flight
to Jeju Island tomorrow.

43:53.213 --> 43:54.340
Bye.

44:50.938 --> 44:51.772
Hey.

44:53.774 --> 44:55.067
Did you stay up all night again?

44:55.150 --> 44:56.568
Yes.

44:56.652 --> 44:58.862
Hold on. Why are you here
so early in the morning?

44:59.446 --> 45:01.073
Let's talk.

45:09.915 --> 45:11.959
Tae-kyung, let's eat.

45:13.710 --> 45:15.045
Goodness.

45:15.129 --> 45:17.256
Tae-kyung, you can
go back to bed after eating.

45:22.678 --> 45:23.720
What?

45:24.221 --> 45:26.098
Where did she go at this hour?

45:43.282 --> 45:44.408
Hello.

45:50.497 --> 45:52.833
You must be exhausted
from working all night.

45:52.916 --> 45:55.043
You could have rested
and met me in the afternoon.

45:55.919 --> 45:58.130
Aren't you signing a contract
with the publisher at noon?

45:58.755 --> 46:01.341
Well, signing it isn't a big deal.

46:02.342 --> 46:03.427
Look.

46:04.595 --> 46:07.598
I looked over the contract
during my spare time,

46:07.681 --> 46:09.933
- and something bothered me.
- What?

46:11.477 --> 46:14.354
It's about this "exclusive publication".

46:14.438 --> 46:15.898
What does this mean?

46:17.232 --> 46:19.067
I'm not entirely sure.

46:20.569 --> 46:21.820
Then how about

46:21.904 --> 46:24.281
this "royalty" part?

46:24.364 --> 46:28.869
It's the amount of money
I'll be receiving.

46:29.912 --> 46:33.624
Then shouldn't Article 11 be revised?

46:37.544 --> 46:40.297
Why should it be?

46:42.925 --> 46:44.051
Well…

46:44.718 --> 46:47.804
- Call the person in charge for me.
- Sorry?

46:56.813 --> 46:59.274
Hello, this is Jin Tae-kyung.

46:59.900 --> 47:01.777
One minute. Here.

47:01.860 --> 47:02.819
Thank you.

47:04.488 --> 47:05.572
Hello?

47:05.656 --> 47:07.616
Well, I called

47:08.116 --> 47:12.079
to ask you about the contract.
Article 11 regarding royalties.

47:12.829 --> 47:14.164
Correct.

47:14.248 --> 47:17.543
I believe the percentage is too low.

47:17.626 --> 47:20.754
She writes and draws everything.
You guys just publish it.

47:21.797 --> 47:22.631
Me?

47:24.967 --> 47:26.760
I'm her manager.

47:28.887 --> 47:29.930
Correct.

47:31.431 --> 47:32.808
Okay, then.

47:32.891 --> 47:34.935
Please call us back after discussing it.

47:35.018 --> 47:35.936
Thank you.

47:37.813 --> 47:41.692
They will discuss the profit percentage
among themselves

47:41.775 --> 47:43.318
and get back to you.

47:43.402 --> 47:44.861
I see.

47:44.945 --> 47:47.739
If something in a contract

47:47.823 --> 47:50.325
bothers you in the future as well,

47:50.409 --> 47:52.244
you have to ask them about it.

47:53.120 --> 47:57.291
You could lose your rights as the creator
depending on what's written.

47:57.374 --> 48:00.294
You need to be meticulous, okay?

48:00.377 --> 48:01.920
I'm a divorcée.

48:04.256 --> 48:05.257
So?

48:06.341 --> 48:07.426
What?

48:08.927 --> 48:10.887
I'm just saying.

48:15.851 --> 48:17.144
There's something

48:17.978 --> 48:19.855
people misunderstand about penguins.

48:19.938 --> 48:21.064
What is it?

48:21.148 --> 48:22.816
They think a male
and a female are cordial.

48:23.734 --> 48:24.735
Is that not true?

48:25.527 --> 48:28.572
I saw how a penguin couple took great care

48:28.655 --> 48:30.866
of their baby in a documentary.

48:30.949 --> 48:32.451
Only during the breeding season.

48:33.035 --> 48:34.786
The next year,

48:34.870 --> 48:37.289
they don't think twice
about mating with other penguins.

48:38.707 --> 48:39.666
But…

48:40.500 --> 48:43.670
why are you telling me this right now?

48:45.255 --> 48:48.050
A divorce is nothing special
in the animal kingdom.

48:54.806 --> 48:56.850
Do you want to have breakfast?

48:57.434 --> 48:58.310
Sure.

49:10.530 --> 49:12.908
What is it? You should eat too.

49:21.458 --> 49:22.668
What is this?

49:26.588 --> 49:28.006
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

49:28.090 --> 49:29.716
Read it through and sign it.

49:37.015 --> 49:39.643
- Honey, this is--
- This isn't a spur-of-the-moment decision.

49:40.227 --> 49:41.436
I thought long and hard.

49:41.520 --> 49:44.147
I wish you would
respect me and my decision.

49:54.908 --> 49:57.744
I'm sorry, Hyang-rae.

49:58.453 --> 50:01.832
I made you raise Bo-mi all by yourself.

50:02.332 --> 50:05.752
I know how lonely you were
while I was away.

50:05.836 --> 50:07.421
I'm truly sorry about that.

50:09.756 --> 50:10.966
But you see…

50:13.176 --> 50:14.720
To an extent, I had no choice.

50:14.803 --> 50:17.639
- It's my job.
- Don't make excuses.

50:18.223 --> 50:21.977
Right. At first, you had no say

50:22.060 --> 50:24.896
when they told you
to go to Busan or Namhae.

50:24.980 --> 50:27.816
But after some time,
you grew to prefer that lifestyle.

50:31.611 --> 50:34.364
You're right. It was wrong of me.

50:35.490 --> 50:38.243
- Who is she?
- Who are you talking about?

50:38.326 --> 50:40.871
The woman who sometimes appears on TV.

50:40.954 --> 50:43.498
- Jin Ha-kyung, was it?
- Director Jin Ha-kyung.

50:43.582 --> 50:45.417
Why? What about her?

50:45.500 --> 50:46.877
I saw it.

50:47.586 --> 50:49.629
I saw you going to her place.

51:03.018 --> 51:05.228
No! It's not what you think.

51:05.729 --> 51:08.356
You're completely misunderstanding.

51:11.985 --> 51:13.195
Look.

51:14.154 --> 51:15.572
It was work-related.

51:15.655 --> 51:17.407
I wasn't the only one there.

51:17.491 --> 51:20.076
There's this forecaster
on our team called Si-woo.

51:20.160 --> 51:23.747
She was kind enough
to let us stay at her place.

51:25.415 --> 51:26.958
It's really not what you think.

51:27.042 --> 51:29.503
You can check with him.

51:29.586 --> 51:32.130
I swear on Bo-mi.

51:32.714 --> 51:34.925
Don't you dare drag her into this.

51:35.842 --> 51:37.260
All right. I won't.

51:38.011 --> 51:39.971
But what you just said is absurd.

51:40.055 --> 51:42.057
You know I wouldn't cheat on you.

51:45.769 --> 51:48.021
Right. That's what I hope.

51:49.105 --> 51:51.107
During our time apart,

51:51.191 --> 51:53.235
I've never suspected you of cheating

51:53.318 --> 51:54.986
because I trusted you.

51:55.737 --> 51:57.614
But when I saw you that day,

51:58.907 --> 52:00.075
it was quite painful.

52:01.159 --> 52:03.495
Fine, Hyang-rae. I…

52:05.622 --> 52:08.333
How long did you stay at home
after coming to Headquarters?

52:08.959 --> 52:12.671
I thought you and Bo-mi
were uncomfortable with my being there.

52:15.048 --> 52:17.008
Don't make excuses, Dong-han.

52:17.092 --> 52:19.719
You chose to run away
because you were uncomfortable.

52:19.803 --> 52:21.429
Don't blame it on us.

52:22.639 --> 52:25.100
Do you even know how I felt that day?

52:28.395 --> 52:29.646
It was

52:30.689 --> 52:32.190
immature of me.

52:39.281 --> 52:41.324
Why do you make me feel so miserable?

52:43.451 --> 52:45.453
What have I ever done to you?

52:50.709 --> 52:52.377
I'm sorry.

52:53.086 --> 52:54.212
Hyang-rae.

52:54.713 --> 52:56.256
I'll move back in right away.

52:56.339 --> 52:58.300
Says who?

52:58.383 --> 53:00.176
Honey, give me one more--

53:00.260 --> 53:01.595
I can't do this anymore.

53:01.678 --> 53:04.973
Just be a man and sign the divorce papers.

53:05.056 --> 53:06.600
Let's get a divorce

53:06.683 --> 53:10.604
and live carefree lives
like we do right now.

53:10.687 --> 53:11.688
Okay?

54:20.340 --> 54:22.801
- What's the patient's name?
- Lee Si-woo.

54:22.884 --> 54:25.345
And what is your relationship?

54:26.805 --> 54:30.350
You see, I'm Lee Si-woo's father.

54:30.433 --> 54:31.977
I'm his guardian.

54:32.936 --> 54:35.730
Go in that direction. He's in Room 305.

54:35.814 --> 54:36.982
Thank you.

54:37.065 --> 54:39.526
By the way, how badly is he hurt?

55:32.245 --> 55:33.413
Are you okay?

55:58.730 --> 56:00.190
I'm okay.

56:07.197 --> 56:08.364
Don't cry.

56:26.216 --> 56:27.133
Hey, Si-woo.

56:28.968 --> 56:31.304
What happened to you? Tell me.

56:31.888 --> 56:33.473
What happened to your eyes?

56:33.556 --> 56:35.475
Tell me what happened.

56:36.643 --> 56:37.894
Is that you, Father?

56:37.977 --> 56:39.938
Yes. It's me. Your father.

56:40.021 --> 56:41.981
Goodness. Look at you.

56:42.065 --> 56:45.360
He's doing worse than I thought.

56:47.028 --> 56:49.405
How did you know I was here? No.

56:49.489 --> 56:51.282
- Why did you come?
- You idiot.

56:51.366 --> 56:53.952
How could I sit still
after hearing that you were hurt?

56:54.035 --> 56:57.163
I couldn't reach you. I was so frustrated

56:57.247 --> 56:59.999
that I barged into your workplace.

57:00.083 --> 57:03.211
- You went there?
- Hey, don't you worry.

57:03.294 --> 57:05.713
I even met the Director General.

57:05.797 --> 57:09.342
I made sure he'd compensate us,
so leave this up to me.

57:09.425 --> 57:11.803
I'll take care of everything, okay?

57:12.470 --> 57:17.725
By the way, did you only hurt your eyes?

57:17.809 --> 57:20.270
Let me see.

57:20.770 --> 57:24.149
Hey, you need to tell me
if you're hurting anywhere else.

57:24.232 --> 57:26.776
We need to be compensated
as much as possible.

57:26.860 --> 57:27.861
Got it?

57:29.696 --> 57:32.240
- Director Jin.
- Yes?

57:32.323 --> 57:33.700
Can you make this man leave?

57:37.662 --> 57:39.330
- Hey, Si-woo.
- Leave.

57:39.414 --> 57:42.000
And go back to Seoul immediately.

57:43.209 --> 57:45.336
What are you talking about?

57:45.420 --> 57:48.089
I should be by your side when you're hurt.

57:48.173 --> 57:50.175
Just leave already!

57:54.179 --> 57:57.056
You little punk. Calm down, will you?

57:57.140 --> 58:00.226
I heard Mr. Lee's guardian was here.

58:00.310 --> 58:04.105
That's right. I'm his father.

58:04.189 --> 58:06.566
Hello, sir.
May I have a word with you outside?

58:06.649 --> 58:07.567
Sure.

58:10.445 --> 58:12.155
- Let's go.
- Okay.

58:21.331 --> 58:22.665
He must be acting that way

58:24.042 --> 58:26.544
because he's worried about you.

58:27.712 --> 58:29.380
He's not someone who would worry

58:30.507 --> 58:32.008
because I got hurt.

58:32.634 --> 58:36.137
He would never come here
because he was worried about his son.

58:36.721 --> 58:39.182
- Si-woo--
- That's the kind of father he is!

58:40.725 --> 58:43.520
You didn't have to bring him here!

59:03.331 --> 59:06.000
I don't know what to say
now that I'm here.

59:06.084 --> 59:08.878
Am I an idiot or what?

59:10.713 --> 59:13.633
He has some burns on his face.

59:15.009 --> 59:16.511
Thankfully, they're not severe.

59:16.594 --> 59:20.473
He won't need surgery,
and there won't be any scars.

59:20.557 --> 59:24.269
But I think he injured
his left cornea during the explosion.

59:24.352 --> 59:26.980
He received treatment,
so we'll keep an eye on him.

59:27.564 --> 59:29.065
He damaged his cornea?

59:30.108 --> 59:33.987
That means
his eyesight has been affected, right?

59:34.070 --> 59:37.365
The treatment was a success,
so we'll have to monitor--

59:37.448 --> 59:38.741
I don't care about that.

59:40.118 --> 59:43.538
"Damage in the left cornea
due to an explosion."

59:44.038 --> 59:47.500
Could you emphasize that in your note?

59:48.376 --> 59:52.463
My son deserves
all the compensation he can get,

59:52.547 --> 59:55.800
and your precious diagnosis
is extremely important.

59:56.676 --> 59:59.596
Do you understand what I'm saying?

01:00:00.930 --> 01:00:02.181
Goodness.

01:00:31.419 --> 01:00:33.504
You should have come alone
if you were worried.

01:00:34.714 --> 01:00:36.090
Si-woo's father

01:00:36.591 --> 01:00:39.510
is nothing more than a leech.

01:00:41.638 --> 01:00:44.557
Si-woo's sick of him,
but he can't get rid of him either.

01:00:44.641 --> 01:00:47.518
He wants to cut him off,
but it doesn't work.

01:00:50.938 --> 01:00:52.899
What most people think is a given

01:00:53.399 --> 01:00:55.401
could be something terrible for Si-woo.

01:01:01.866 --> 01:01:03.743
Hey, Ms. Director.

01:01:05.453 --> 01:01:06.913
Here you were.

01:01:08.331 --> 01:01:09.791
What will you do about my son?

01:01:13.294 --> 01:01:15.296
I just spoke with his doctor.

01:01:17.090 --> 01:01:18.508
He could lose his sight.

01:01:20.468 --> 01:01:21.594
His sight?

01:01:21.678 --> 01:01:23.805
He damaged his cornea.

01:01:23.888 --> 01:01:25.056
What will you do?

01:01:25.139 --> 01:01:28.559
That young kid has gone blind now.

01:01:29.977 --> 01:01:31.479
Keep this in mind.

01:01:31.562 --> 01:01:34.440
You better give
a hefty compensation, or else.

01:01:35.274 --> 01:01:38.528
Don't try to be sly
and cut down on the amount.

01:01:38.611 --> 01:01:41.614
If you do, I'll contact the Blue House

01:01:41.698 --> 01:01:43.616
and post about this online.

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:44.742
Got it?

01:01:45.827 --> 01:01:47.662
If that happens,

01:01:49.080 --> 01:01:53.626
either you or the Director General
will get sacked. Right?

01:01:54.502 --> 01:01:57.422
So don't turn this into a big deal.

01:01:57.505 --> 01:02:00.591
Just give me the compensation. Got that?

01:02:04.846 --> 01:02:06.514
You can talk with me about that.

01:02:09.600 --> 01:02:11.394
Why do you keep butting in?

01:02:11.477 --> 01:02:13.563
I'm Han Ki-jun,
a spokesperson for the KMA.

01:02:14.147 --> 01:02:16.190
I usually deal with the press.

01:02:16.274 --> 01:02:18.693
But there are also times
when I deal with people like you.

01:02:18.776 --> 01:02:20.528
And this is why I came here.

01:02:24.490 --> 01:02:26.367
- Let's go.
- Damn it!

01:02:27.243 --> 01:02:28.536
I don't want to hear it.

01:02:28.619 --> 01:02:30.580
Just call the Director General

01:02:30.663 --> 01:02:33.666
and tell him
to get the money ready. Go on.

01:02:34.167 --> 01:02:36.461
Hurry up!

01:02:36.544 --> 01:02:39.464
I demand at least 30 million won.

01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:40.548
Got that?

01:02:41.048 --> 01:02:42.467
Hurry up and call him.

01:02:42.550 --> 01:02:43.926
- Go on.
- That's enough!

01:02:45.052 --> 01:02:46.220
What?

01:02:47.138 --> 01:02:48.139
Hey.

01:02:51.684 --> 01:02:54.061
- Let's go.
- Hey.

01:02:54.145 --> 01:02:56.898
Hey! You fool.

01:02:56.981 --> 01:02:59.108
You should be lying in bed

01:02:59.192 --> 01:03:01.611
if you got injured.

01:03:02.153 --> 01:03:05.448
- Come with me.
- I'm not letting go of this opportunity.

01:03:05.531 --> 01:03:06.824
Right.

01:03:06.908 --> 01:03:08.659
This is a great opportunity for you.

01:03:08.743 --> 01:03:09.911
- Right?
- What did you say?

01:03:09.994 --> 01:03:11.996
What's the money for this time?

01:03:12.580 --> 01:03:14.749
Gambling? Scamming?

01:03:14.832 --> 01:03:15.792
Women?

01:03:15.875 --> 01:03:17.335
What is it this time?

01:03:17.418 --> 01:03:20.254
- You little--
- You embarrass me!

01:03:23.841 --> 01:03:25.802
So please.

01:03:26.636 --> 01:03:29.555
- Just disappear from my sight!
- How dare you?

01:03:56.040 --> 01:03:57.500
Damn it.

01:04:04.674 --> 01:04:05.758
Don't forget.

01:04:06.676 --> 01:04:08.094
I want 30 million won.

01:04:08.970 --> 01:04:10.054
Thirty million.

01:04:23.276 --> 01:04:24.944
So you didn't come here to see me.

01:04:25.611 --> 01:04:27.780
- What?
- Right?

01:04:29.991 --> 01:04:31.075
Well…

01:04:37.623 --> 01:04:38.875
Yu-jin.

01:04:58.978 --> 01:05:00.897
Typhoon Ricky, the 14th typhoon,

01:05:00.980 --> 01:05:03.691
is crossing Korea
at a speed of 30m per second.

01:05:06.485 --> 01:05:07.778
Let's talk.

01:05:10.239 --> 01:05:11.532
I want to talk.

01:05:15.578 --> 01:05:17.079
First of all, I'm sorry

01:05:17.163 --> 01:05:19.290
for bringing him here without telling you.

01:05:19.373 --> 01:05:20.875
- But--
- Some things in this world

01:05:21.459 --> 01:05:23.210
are just impossible.

01:05:25.171 --> 01:05:27.798
Just like how humans
can't change a typhoon's course,

01:05:29.008 --> 01:05:31.302
the same goes
for my relationship with my father.

01:05:32.261 --> 01:05:33.930
It can never…

01:05:35.181 --> 01:05:36.724
be changed.

01:05:38.851 --> 01:05:40.853
I stay true to myself

01:05:41.479 --> 01:05:43.356
just like you do.

01:05:48.903 --> 01:05:50.738
You told me to think about it.

01:05:53.532 --> 01:05:55.201
So I did.

01:05:59.538 --> 01:06:01.165
I don't think I can do it.

01:06:02.124 --> 01:06:04.043
What are you saying?

01:06:09.507 --> 01:06:13.344
When a hot typhoon changes

01:06:13.427 --> 01:06:16.180
as it passes through Korea's cold air

01:06:17.598 --> 01:06:21.477
we call it a variation area.

01:06:26.816 --> 01:06:28.275
I'll let you go.

01:06:29.902 --> 01:06:31.654
So run away from me.

01:06:35.700 --> 01:06:40.413
Lee Si-woo, a hot typhoon,
met me, the cold air.

01:06:40.496 --> 01:06:41.706
And then,

01:06:42.707 --> 01:06:45.960
he eventually bid farewell to me.

01:06:56.721 --> 01:06:57.888
I'm sorry

01:06:58.848 --> 01:07:00.182
that this is all I'm worth.

01:07:04.103 --> 01:07:05.312
Let's…

01:07:08.774 --> 01:07:10.026
break up.

01:07:21.454 --> 01:07:23.039
How did we end up

01:07:24.457 --> 01:07:27.001
looking down a path with no knowledge

01:07:27.084 --> 01:07:29.086
of what awaits us?

01:08:02.661 --> 01:08:04.038
Go back to the hospital right now.

01:08:04.121 --> 01:08:06.499
I have no problem working.

01:08:06.582 --> 01:08:08.167
Is there a way for us to know sooner?

01:08:08.250 --> 01:08:09.877
We could launch a sonde
at the eastern side of Jeju

01:08:09.960 --> 01:08:11.420
and at the sea west of the island.

01:08:11.504 --> 01:08:15.549
I'm sure you know it's highly dangerous
in these weather conditions.

01:08:16.133 --> 01:08:18.427
There's no such thing
as an accurate forecast.

01:08:18.511 --> 01:08:20.179
We can only make predictions.

01:08:20.262 --> 01:08:22.139
- Three, two, one.
- Even if they're just predictions,

01:08:22.223 --> 01:08:23.849
I believe it is our duty to use

01:08:23.933 --> 01:08:26.393
the most accurate data possible
to make such predictions.

01:08:28.104 --> 01:08:30.314
You and I are married.
That's our conclusion.

01:08:30.397 --> 01:08:31.774
So tell me if you regret it.

01:08:31.857 --> 01:08:33.400
Did you make my daughter cry?

01:08:33.484 --> 01:08:34.819
Sir, it's not what you think.

01:08:34.902 --> 01:08:37.780
I don't think I can do this.

01:08:37.863 --> 01:08:39.198
I can't see you, Tae-kyung.

01:08:39.281 --> 01:08:41.325
Let's break up, Si-woo.

01:08:43.786 --> 01:08:48.582
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
